# File spec for ./package_yaml.rhai — the shared script-side package.yaml gate shipped in
# the agent image. Importers keep their own lanes (/agent/src/package/build.sdd,
# /agent/src/package/update.sdd restate the caller side); this spec freezes only the module.

Spec: LibPackageYaml

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Give the package build and update lanes one shared gate for the author-facing
    `package.yaml`: take a decoded manifest map, inject the missing `apiVersion`/`kind`/
    `requirements` defaults with warnings, force the few keys no author may omit
    (`metadata.name`/`category`/`type` strings, a map `options`, an array `requirements`),
    and rewrite the `options` section into JSON-schema-shaped property definitions,
    returning the patched map for the Rust-side load or the in-place manifest rewrite.

Exposes:
  @validate(yaml) — the gate, reached by importers as @pck::validate(yaml) (the
    `import "package_yaml" as pck` convention frozen in ./../packages/build.rhai and
    ./../packages/update.rhai). In-memory only, returns the patched map.
  @properties_improve(values) — the options-property rewriter @validate runs on every
    present `options`; recursion over nested `object` properties; tests in
    ./../../tests/rhai_lib.rs also call it directly as `pkg::properties_improve`.
  @get_json_type(val) — the `type_of`→JSON-type-name guesser used by @properties_improve's
    default-inference legs.

Accepts:
  @validate — a decoded manifest map: the build lane feeds @yaml_decode's plain @rhai map,
    the update lane feeds `yaml_decode_ordered`'s @YamlDoc (dot-accessee debate in Tasks).
  @properties_improve — any @Dynamic; a non-map value never enters the loop and a fresh
    empty `#{}` comes back instead (the `else {{}}` arm discards the input).
  @get_json_type — any @Dynamic to be typed.
  Nothing shape-checks its inputs first: every key read is preceded by `"k" in x.keys()`
    and the lone array index `default[0]` is guarded by `default.len() > 0`, so rhai's
    map-miss `()` and array out-of-range throws are never exercised by this file.

Returns:
  @validate — the patched map: `apiVersion`/`kind` injected only when absent, `requirements`
    injected as `[]` only when absent, `options` replaced by the @properties_improve result;
    other keys (`images`, `resources`, …) passed through byte-for-byte. Importers rebind
    through the return value (`yaml = pck::validate(yaml)`).
  @properties_improve — the input map with its improvements applied.
  @get_json_type — one of the literals `string`, `object`, `array`, `boolean`, `integer`,
    `number`.

Raises:
  Script `throw`s, verbatim (`${…}` interpolates at runtime):
    - `No metadata defined in package.yaml`
    - `No metadata.${key} defined in package.yaml` — one text per key, only the first
      failing key of `["name", "category", "type"]` is ever reported
    - `metadata.${key} should be a string`
    - `options should be a map.`
    - `requirements should be an array.`
    - `no type and no default for property ${prop}`
    - `Invalid type "${values[prop].type}" for property ${prop}`
    - `property ${prop} is an array with no items definition and not enough values in default to guess.`
  Engine raises, unguarded — interpreter errors, not script throws:
    - `yaml.keys()` when @validate receives a non-map.
    - `.keys()` on a scalar `metadata` or a non-map `options` property entry.
    - @get_json_type's `switch` has no catch-all arm, so any @type_of outside its six
      (`()`, `u64`, `char`, …) fails the switch itself rather than throwing a reviewed text.

Handles:
  Missing `apiVersion` / `kind` — @log_warn `You should set your apiVersion` /
    `You should set your kind`, then inject `vinyl.solidite.fr/v1beta1` / `Package`;
    warn-and-continue, never a throw.
  `options` absent — the whole gate-to-improve branch is skipped.
  `type` invalid where a `default` exists — silently repaired from the inferred type and
    never reported; the `Invalid type …` throw is only reachable with `type` invalid and
    `default` absent, `no type and no default …` only with both absent.
  `object` without `properties` — synthesised from `default`'s keys when present, else
    kept `#{}` behind @log_warn `Properties definition left empty for property ${prop}`.
  `array` without `items` and a non-empty `default` — `items` guessed from `default[0]`
    only; first entry `object` seeds `items.properties` from its keys and recurses.

Must:
  Read exactly `apiVersion`, `kind`, `metadata` with `metadata.name`/`metadata.category`/
    `metadata.type`, `options` and `requirements`; `description`, `features`, `images`,
    `resources`, `recommandations`, `value_script` are never read or checked — the Rust
    @VynilPackageSource load (./../../../common/src/vynilpackage.sdd) is the gate for those.
  Require @type_of `string` for the three metadata keys, checked in the loop order
    `name`, `category`, `type`.
  Never validate the value of a present `apiVersion` or `kind` — defaults only; the
    misspelled `vinyl.solidite.fr/v1beta1` ships from this file's @line-4 assignment and
    no code path here compares it against anything.
  Keep `valid_type` exactly `["string", "object", "array", "boolean", "integer", "number"]`
    and the guess map exactly string→`string`, map→`object`, array→`array`, bool→`boolean`,
    i64→`integer`, f64→`number`; all six guesses are members of `valid_type`, so an
    inferred type can never trip the `Invalid type` throw.
  Compute object parent defaults thus: recurse `properties` first (synthesised or
    authored), then set the parent `default` only when it has none, gather only children
    that carry a `default` (partial accepted), and set nothing when the computed map is
    empty — an authored parent `default` is never overwritten.
  Accept a present `items` on an `array` untouched — no validation, no recursion, unlike
    the synthesised path, and only the first `default` element shapes a synthesised
    items entry; no sibling element is sampled.
  Stay import-clean: no `import` of any module, no top-level statements (importing the
    module evaluates nothing), no fs/k8s/OCI/registry calls — @log_warn is the only engine
    surface the file calls.

Depends on:
  wynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — @log_warn from the core engine registrar, the script-side
    helpers installed by @Script::new_core's base
    (./../../../common/src/rhaihandler.sdd); rhai builtins (@type_of, `switch`, map/array
    indexing, `in`) arrive with the engine and nothing else is reached.
  ./../packages/build.rhai — imports this as `pck`, runs @validate on `yaml_decode` of the
    source manifest before staging (./../../src/package/build.sdd lane).
  ./../packages/update.rhai — imports this as `pck`, runs @validate on a
    `yaml_decode_ordered` @YamlDoc on the tag-only write pass
    (./../../src/package/update.sdd lane).

References:
  ./../../src/package/update.sdd — caller-side restatement of this gate and the home of
    the `[?]` deciding whether the misspelled default ships; ./../../src/package/build.sdd —
    the staging lane this gate serves.
  ./../../../common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — the Rust accept/reject surface the gate
    partially previews; ./../../../common/src/yamlhandler.sdd — @YamlDoc's registered
    surface behind the Tasks dot-access question.

Tasks:
  [x] Cover @properties_improve's parent-default leg on the mock @Script::new_mock engine
      in ./../../tests/rhai_lib.rs — five `package_yaml_properties_improve_*` tests map it.
  [ ] Cover @validate: no test imports the gate at all — injections, @log_warn lines and
      all eight throw texts are unmapped; ./../../tests/rhai_build.rs never reaches this
      module (mock `security_filter`/push/sign only).
  [ ] Cover the array-guess, non-map-entry and dead-switch legs: `items` guessed from
      `default[0]` (scalar and object first entries), the guessless-array throw, and
      @get_json_type's six mappings plus its no-arm failure on `()`/`u64` defaults.
  [?] Dot access versus @YamlDoc: the body mutates and reads via map dotted syntax
      (`yaml.apiVersion = …`, `values[prop].type`, even the bracketed `values[prop]`
      indexer), but the update lane hands it a @YamlDoc with only `[]` indexers and named
      member functions registered (@YamlDoc in ./../../../common/src/yamlhandler.sdd) —
      whether the tag-only pass reaches @validate at all, or dies first on an
      engine property error, must be settled by a test on a `yaml_decode_ordered` input
      (pairs with ./../../src/package/update.sdd's chained-write `[?]`).
  [?] `vinyl.solidite.fr/v1beta1` mixes the `vinyl` misspelling and a `v1beta1` beside the
      CRD group `vynil.solidite.fr/v1`; shipped packages, docs and the box manifest
      already carry it and no Rust path validates the value, so renaming is wire-facing.
      The keep-or-fix decision lives in ./../../src/package/update.sdd — do not fork it here.
  [?] A no-default `switch` makes an unguessable `default` (YAML null → `()`) an opaque
      engine failure mid-validation. Decide whether @get_json_type gains a catch-all or
      @properties_improve a scripted throw.
  [?] Freeze-or-fix the array asymmetry: an authored `items` is waved through unchecked
      while a synthesised one is inferred from `default[0]` only — first element shape is
      treated as whole-array truth.
  [ ] Carry the file's own TODOs forward or retire them: requirement list items pass with
      any content once `requirements` is an array, and `options` auto_improvements are
      limited to the type/default legs documented above.

Done when:
  @validate and @get_json_type have mapped mock-engine tests pinning the injections and
    the verbatim throws, the dot-access and misspelling questions are decided (the latter
    once, under ./../../src/package/update.sdd), and the five existing
    `package_yaml_properties_improve_*` tests plus `cargo test -p agent` stay green.

Scenario: deficient header is patched with warnings
  Given a map with `metadata` carrying `name`, `category` and `type` strings but no
    `apiVersion`, `kind` or `requirements`
  When @validate runs
  Then `log_warn` fires for the two missing headers, `apiVersion` is injected as
    `vinyl.solidite.fr/v1beta1`, `kind` as `Package`, `requirements` as `[]`
  And the same map is returned unthrown, all other keys untouched
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: metadata gate reports the first offender
  Given `metadata` absent → throw `No metadata defined in package.yaml`
  Given `metadata` without `category` → throw `No metadata.category defined in package.yaml`
  Given `metadata.type: 3` → throw `metadata.type should be a string`
  Given `metadata` a bare string → no scripted outcome: the `.keys()` call raises as an
    engine error, `metadata` itself is never type-checked
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: options gate and improve ride back through validate
  Given `options: "x"` → throw `options should be a map.`
  Given an options property `{type: "str", "default": "hi"}` → `type` silently becomes
    `string`, the invalid name never reported
  Given the same property with no `default` → throw `Invalid type "str" for property <prop>`
  Given a property with neither `type` nor `default` → throw
    `no type and no default for property <prop>`
  Given `options: #{myobj: #{type: "object"}}` → `properties` synthesised as `#{}` with
    `log_warn Properties definition left empty for property myobj`
  No mapped test exists for the @validate leg.

Scenario: leaf defaults compute the parent default
  Given an `object` property whose children carry all / some / no defaults, one whose
    parent already owns a `default`, and one nested three levels deep
  When @properties_improve runs
  Then the parent `default` is computed, or partial (only children with defaults appear),
    or absent when no child has one, never overwritten, and cascades child→parent level
    by level
  Maps to tests @package_yaml_properties_improve_leaf_defaults_all_children_compute_parent_default,
    @package_yaml_properties_improve_leaf_defaults_partial_children_compute_partial_default,
    @package_yaml_properties_improve_leaf_defaults_no_children_default_means_no_parent_default,
    @package_yaml_properties_improve_existing_parent_default_not_overwritten,
    @package_yaml_properties_improve_leaf_defaults_cascade_multiple_levels

Scenario: array items guessed from the first default entry
  Given an `array` property with no `items` and `default` `["a", "b"]`
  When @properties_improve runs
  Then `items.type` is `string` (from the first entry) and later entries are ignored
  And with an object first entry, `items.properties` is seeded from that entry's keys and
    recursively improved
  And with `default` absent or empty (`[]`), the run throws
    `property <prop> is an array with no items definition and not enough values in default to guess.`
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: ungessable defaults kill the switch
  Given a property `{ "default": ... }` whose value types as `()` or any @rhai type
    outside the six arms
  When @get_json_type runs
  Then execution ends in the engine's no-switch-match error, not one of the module's
    throw texts
  No mapped test exists.
